Here is a csh script that gives the total of all the scores  and the number
of games for each nethack player as listed in the record file. .

It was written to work for nethack 3.0 versions only.  The list prints out
in alphabetical order.  You can optionally specify a list of names to be
displayed by specifying them as arguments on the command line.  The default
is to display all players recorded in the record file.  I call the script
"nhtotals", but you can call it what you want.  Remember, scripts require 
execution privileges.  Enjoy!

    usage: nhtotals [players...]

Ross Wille - Hewlett Packard
wille@hpda.hp.com

P.S. No flames about what a lousy script writer I am!  *<B-)
----------------------------- C U T   H E R E -------------------------------
#!/bin/csh
set nh='/usr/games/nethack'	# change this to the location of your nethack
if ($1 == '') then
    set names='all'
else
    set names="$argv"
endif
set players=`$nh -s $names | awk '/-/&&\\!/:/ {print substr($3,1,length($3)-2)}' | sort -u`
echo 'nethack score totals:'
foreach player ($players)
    set total=`$nh -s $player | awk '/-/&&\\!/:/ {s += $2} END {print s}'`
    set games=`$nh -s $player | awk '/-/&&\\!/:/ {s++} END {print s}'`
    echo $player $total $games | awk '{printf("  %-10s%7d (%d)\n",$1,$2,$3)}'
end


